-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter XV (ss 361-368): PUBLIC BENEFIT CORPORATIONS.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone (src:1781-1828).
--
-- Quote lines are slices of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text): `-- src:N | ...` is line N.
--
-- Subchapter XV is outside the stockholder-to-member reading for a nonprofit nonstock corporation (s 114(c)(3)); s 363
-- says what happens to a nonprofit nonstock corporation that meets a public benefit corporation.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation: here, an incorporator, a
-- director or a stockholder (including a minority stockholder) of a public benefit corporation, or someone who
-- acquires its stock.

§ `Subchapter XV. Public Benefit Corporations`

§§ `s 361 Law applicable to public benefit corporations; how formed`

-- src:1784 | This subchapter applies to all public benefit corporations, as defined in § 362 of this title. If a corporation elects to become a public benefit corporation under this subchapter in the manner prescribed in this subchapter, it shall be subject in all respects to the provisions of this chapter, except to the extent this subchapter imposes additional or different requirements, in which case such requirements shall apply.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 361 (src:1784)
GIVEN `the corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 361 this subchapter applies to the corporation` `the corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362` MEANS
    `the corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362`

-- "it shall be subject in all respects to the provisions of this chapter, except to the extent this subchapter imposes
-- additional or different requirements, in which case such requirements shall apply." A corporation that is not a
-- public benefit corporation is outside the section: not covered.
-- src:1784 | This subchapter applies to all public benefit corporations, as defined in § 362 of this title. If a corporation elects to become a public benefit corporation under this subchapter in the manner prescribed in this subchapter, it shall be subject in all respects to the provisions of this chapter, except to the extent this subchapter imposes additional or different requirements, in which case such requirements shall apply.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 361 (src:1784)
GIVEN `the corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this subchapter imposes an additional or different requirement on the point` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361 the requirement of this subchapter applies in place of the requirement of this chapter` `the corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362` `this subchapter imposes an additional or different requirement on the point` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362`
    THEN JUST `this subchapter imposes an additional or different requirement on the point`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 362 Public benefit corporation defined; contents of certificate of incorporation`

-- (a): "a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the requirements of this chapter that is intended to
-- produce a public benefit or public benefits and to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner". The two
-- certificate requirements that follow ("In the certificate of incorporation, a public benefit corporation shall: (1) ...
-- (2) ...") are rules about the certificate, not part of what makes the corporation one (fork F20).
-- src:1788 | A “public benefit corporation” is a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the requirements of this chapter that is intended to produce a public benefit or public benefits and to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(a) (src:1788)
DECLARE `s 362(a) Corporation said to be a public benefit corporation` HAS
    `the corporation is a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the requirements of this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation is intended to produce a public benefit or public benefits`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation is intended to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner`                              IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1788 | A “public benefit corporation” is a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the requirements of this chapter that is intended to produce a public benefit or public benefits and to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(a) (src:1788)
GIVEN corporation IS A `s 362(a) Corporation said to be a public benefit corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(a) the corporation is a public benefit corporation` corporation MEANS
        corporation's `the corporation is a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the requirements of this chapter`
    AND corporation's `the corporation is intended to produce a public benefit or public benefits`
    AND corporation's `the corporation is intended to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner`

-- "To that end, a public benefit corporation shall be managed in a manner that balances the stockholders' pecuniary
-- interests, the best interests of those materially affected by the corporation's conduct, and the public benefit or
-- public benefits identified in its certificate of incorporation." (Also the content of s 365(a).)
-- src:1788 | To that end, a public benefit corporation shall be managed in a manner that balances the stockholders’ pecuniary interests, the best interests of those materially affected by the corporation’s conduct, and the public benefit or public benefits identified in its certificate of incorporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(a) (src:1788)
DECLARE `s 362(a) Balancing of interests` HAS
    `the stockholders' pecuniary interests are balanced`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the best interests of those materially affected by the corporation's conduct are balanced`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation are balanced`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1788 | To that end, a public benefit corporation shall be managed in a manner that balances the stockholders’ pecuniary interests, the best interests of those materially affected by the corporation’s conduct, and the public benefit or public benefits identified in its certificate of incorporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(a) (src:1788)
GIVEN balancing IS A `s 362(a) Balancing of interests`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(a) the corporation is managed in a manner that balances the three interests` balancing MEANS
        balancing's `the stockholders' pecuniary interests are balanced`
    AND balancing's `the best interests of those materially affected by the corporation's conduct are balanced`
    AND balancing's `the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation are balanced`

-- (a)(1): "Identify within its statement of business or purpose pursuant to s 102(a)(3) of this title one or more
-- specific public benefits to be promoted by the corporation".
-- src:1789 | (1) Identify within its statement of business or purpose pursuant to § 102(a)(3) of this title one or more specific public benefits to be promoted by the corporation; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(a)(1) (src:1789)
GIVEN `the number of specific public benefits that the statement of business or purpose in the certificate of incorporation identifies` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 102(a)(3) (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(a)(1) the certificate identifies within its statement of business or purpose one or more specific public benefits` `the number of specific public benefits that the statement of business or purpose in the certificate of incorporation identifies` MEANS
    `the number of specific public benefits that the statement of business or purpose in the certificate of incorporation identifies` AT LEAST 1

-- src:1790 | (2) State within its heading that it is a public benefit corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(a)(2) (src:1790)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation states within its heading that the corporation is a public benefit corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(a)(2) the certificate states within its heading that it is a public benefit corporation` `the certificate of incorporation states within its heading that the corporation is a public benefit corporation` MEANS
    `the certificate of incorporation states within its heading that the corporation is a public benefit corporation`

-- (b): "a positive effect (or reduction of negative effects) on 1 or more categories of persons, entities, communities
-- or interests (other than stockholders in their capacities as stockholders) including, but not limited to, effects of
-- an artistic, charitable, cultural, ... nature". The list of natures is illustrative and does not limit.
-- src:1791 | “Public benefit” means a positive effect (or reduction of negative effects) on 1 or more categories of persons, entities, communities or interests (other than stockholders in their capacities as stockholders) …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(b) (src:1791)
GIVEN `the effect is a positive effect or a reduction of negative effects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effect is on 1 or more categories of persons, entities, communities or interests other than stockholders in their capacities as stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(b) the effect is a public benefit` `the effect is a positive effect or a reduction of negative effects` `the effect is on 1 or more categories of persons, entities, communities or interests other than stockholders in their capacities as stockholders` MEANS
        `the effect is a positive effect or a reduction of negative effects`
    AND `the effect is on 1 or more categories of persons, entities, communities or interests other than stockholders in their capacities as stockholders`

-- src:1791 | “Public benefit provisions” means the provisions of a certificate of incorporation contemplated by this subchapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(b) (src:1791)
GIVEN `the provision of the certificate of incorporation is one contemplated by this subchapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(b) the provision is a public benefit provision` `the provision of the certificate of incorporation is one contemplated by this subchapter` MEANS
    `the provision of the certificate of incorporation is one contemplated by this subchapter`

-- (c): the name designations deemed to satisfy s 102(a)(1)(i).
-- src:1792 | The name of the public benefit corporation may contain the words “public benefit corporation,” or the abbreviation “P.B.C.,” or the designation “PBC,” which shall be deemed to satisfy the requirements of § 102(a)(1)(i) of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(c) (src:1792)
GIVEN `the name contains the words "public benefit corporation"` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name contains the abbreviation "P.B.C."` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name contains the designation "PBC"` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(c) the name is deemed to satisfy the requirements of s 102(a)(1)(i)` `the name contains the words "public benefit corporation"` `the name contains the abbreviation "P.B.C."` `the name contains the designation "PBC"` MEANS
        `the name contains the words "public benefit corporation"`
    OR  `the name contains the abbreviation "P.B.C."`
    OR  `the name contains the designation "PBC"`

-- "If the name does not contain such language, the corporation shall, prior to issuing unissued shares of stock or
-- disposing of treasury shares, provide notice to any person to whom such stock is issued or who acquires such
-- treasury shares that it is a public benefit corporation; provided that such notice need not be provided if the
-- issuance or disposal is pursuant to an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933 or if, at the time of
-- issuance or disposal, the corporation has a class of securities that is registered under the Securities Exchange
-- Act of 1934." (Both federal Acts are not among the inputs.)
-- src:1792 | If the name does not contain such language, the corporation shall, prior to issuing unissued shares of stock or disposing of treasury shares, provide notice to any person to whom such stock is issued or who acquires such treasury shares that it is a public benefit corporation; provided that such notice need not be provided if the issuance or disposal is pursuant to an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933 [15 U.S.C. § 77r et seq.] or if, at the time of issuance or disposal, the corporation has a class of securities that is registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 362(c) (src:1792)
GIVEN `the corporation is issuing unissued shares of stock or disposing of treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is deemed to satisfy the requirements of s 102(a)(1)(i) under s 362(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuance or disposal is pursuant to an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of issuance or disposal the corporation has a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(c) the corporation must give notice that it is a public benefit corporation to the person who acquires the stock` `the corporation is issuing unissued shares of stock or disposing of treasury shares` `the name is deemed to satisfy the requirements of s 102(a)(1)(i) under s 362(c)` `the issuance or disposal is pursuant to an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933` `at the time of issuance or disposal the corporation has a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934` MEANS
        `the corporation is issuing unissued shares of stock or disposing of treasury shares`
    AND (NOT `the name is deemed to satisfy the requirements of s 102(a)(1)(i) under s 362(c)`)
    AND (NOT `the issuance or disposal is pursuant to an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933`)
    AND (NOT `at the time of issuance or disposal the corporation has a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934`)

§§ `s 363 Nonprofit nonstock corporations`

-- "A nonprofit nonstock corporation may not be a constituent corporation to any merger or consolidation with a public
-- benefit corporation or in which the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation is amended to include
-- a provision authorized by s 362(a)(1)." Nonprofit nonstock includes a charitable one (s 114(d)(3)). Any other
-- corporation, or a merger of another kind, is outside the section: not covered.
-- src:1796 | A nonprofit nonstock corporation may not be a constituent corporation to any merger or consolidation with a public benefit corporation or in which the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation is amended to include a provision authorized by § 362 (a)(1) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 363 (src:1796)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the merger or consolidation is with a public benefit corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation is amended to include a provision authorized by s 362(a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363 the corporation may be a constituent corporation to the merger or consolidation` kind `the merger or consolidation is with a public benefit corporation` `the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation is amended to include a provision authorized by s 362(a)(1)` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` kind AND (`the merger or consolidation is with a public benefit corporation` OR `the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation is amended to include a provision authorized by s 362(a)(1)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

