GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 364 the notice meets the requirement to state that the corporation is a public benefit corporation` `the notice given pursuant to s 151(f) states conspicuously that the corporation is a public benefit corporation formed pursuant to this subchapter` MEANS
    `the notice given pursuant to s 151(f) states conspicuously that the corporation is a public benefit corporation formed pursuant to this subchapter`

§§ `s 365 Duties of directors`

-- (a): the same balance as the second sentence of s 362(a), laid on the board.
-- src:1804 | (a) The board of directors shall manage or direct the business and affairs of the public benefit corporation in a manner that balances the pecuniary interests of the stockholders, the best interests of those materially affected by the corporation’s conduct, and the specific public benefit or public benefits identified in its certificate of incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 365(a) (src:1804)
GIVEN balancing IS A `s 362(a) Balancing of interests`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 365(a) the board manages or directs the business and affairs in a manner that balances the three interests` balancing MEANS
    `s 362(a) the corporation is managed in a manner that balances the three interests` balancing

-- (b): "shall not, by virtue of the public benefit provisions or s 362(a), have any duty to any person on account of
-- any interest of such person in the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation
-- or on account of any interest materially affected by the corporation's conduct". A duty from some other source is
-- not covered.
-- src:1805 | A director of a public benefit corporation shall not, by virtue of the public benefit provisions or § 362(a) of this title, have any duty to any person on account of any interest of such person in the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation or on account of any interest materially affected by the corporation’s conduct …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 365(b) (src:1805)
GIVEN `the duty would be on account of the person's interest in the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duty would be on account of an interest materially affected by the corporation's conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 365(b) the director has a duty to the person by virtue of the public benefit provisions or s 362(a)` `the duty would be on account of the person's interest in the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation` `the duty would be on account of an interest materially affected by the corporation's conduct` MEANS
    IF `the duty would be on account of the person's interest in the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation` OR `the duty would be on account of an interest materially affected by the corporation's conduct`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "with respect to a decision implicating the balance requirement in subsection (a) of this section, will be deemed to
-- satisfy such director's fiduciary duties to stockholders and the corporation if such director's decision is both
-- informed and disinterested and not such that no person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve." Whether a
-- person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve is a judgment the text leaves to whoever applies it (fork F21).
-- Where the conditions are not made out the section does not say the duties are broken: not covered.
-- src:1805 | and, with respect to a decision implicating the balance requirement in subsection (a) of this section, will be deemed to satisfy such director’s fiduciary duties to stockholders and the corporation if such director’s decision is both informed and disinterested and not such that no person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 365(b) (src:1805)
GIVEN `the decision implicates the balance requirement in s 365(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is informed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is disinterested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is such that no person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 365(b) the director is deemed to satisfy the director's fiduciary duties to the stockholders and the corporation` `the decision implicates the balance requirement in s 365(a)` `the decision is informed` `the decision is disinterested` `the decision is such that no person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve` MEANS
    IF        `the decision implicates the balance requirement in s 365(a)`
          AND `the decision is informed`
          AND `the decision is disinterested`
          AND (NOT `the decision is such that no person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (c) first sentence: "A director's ownership of or other interest in the stock of the public benefit corporation
-- shall not alone ... create a conflict of interest ... except to the extent that such ownership or interest would
-- create a conflict of interest if the corporation were not a public benefit corporation."
-- src:1806 | A director’s ownership of or other interest in the stock of the public benefit corporation shall not alone, for the purposes of this section, create a conflict of interest on the part of the director with respect to the director’s decision implicating the balancing requirement in subsection (a) of this section, except to the extent that such ownership or interest would create a conflict of interest if the corporation were not a public benefit corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 365(c) (src:1806)
GIVEN `the ownership or interest would create a conflict of interest if the corporation were not a public benefit corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 365(c) the director's ownership of or interest in the stock creates a conflict of interest for the balancing decision` `the ownership or interest would create a conflict of interest if the corporation were not a public benefit corporation` MEANS
    `the ownership or interest would create a conflict of interest if the corporation were not a public benefit corporation`

-- (c) second sentence: "In the absence of a conflict of interest, no failure to satisfy that balancing requirement
-- shall, for the purposes of s 102(b)(7) or s 145 of this title, constitute an act or omission not in good faith, or a
-- breach of the duty of loyalty, unless the certificate of incorporation so provides." With a conflict, or where the
-- certificate so provides, the section does not answer: not covered.
-- src:1806 | In the absence of a conflict of interest, no failure to satisfy that balancing requirement shall, for the purposes of § 102(b)(7) or § 145 of this title, constitute an act or omission not in good faith, or a breach of the duty of loyalty, unless the certificate of incorporation so provides.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 365(c) (src:1806)
GIVEN `there is a conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation so provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 365(c) a failure to satisfy the balancing requirement is an act or omission not in good faith, or a breach of the duty of loyalty, for the purposes of s 102(b)(7) or s 145` `there is a conflict of interest` `the certificate of incorporation so provides` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there is a conflict of interest`) AND (NOT `the certificate of incorporation so provides`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

